    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSUBSTANTIAL PRICE REDUCTION\n\nThis traditional style cottage with an adjacent derelict stone outbuilding is located in the townland of Roe Kilmeena, a quiet countryside area approximately 6.4 kilometres from Westport town. \n\nWith a floor area of approximately 73.3 sq m/789 sq ft, accommodation comprises of entrance porch, spacious living room, kitchen, utility room, two bedrooms and a bathroom.\n\nThe cottage is in need of refurbishment and modernisation throughout but offers great potential for a wide range of buyers. We believe the property should qualify for the Vacant Homes Refurbishment Grant.\n\nExternally the site extends to approximately 0.47 acres. There is a stone outbuilding to the side of the cottage. \n\nRoe, Kilmeena is a peaceful area within easy reach of Westport and Newport towns and all their many amenities, being eight minute drive from both. Fahy National School is just a 4 minute drive away, making it ideal for families. \n\nOffers in Excess 199,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 2.0m x 2.0m\nTiled floor\n\nLiving Room - 5.0m x 4.8m\nTiled floor, fireplace, hotpress\n\nKitchen - 3.6m x 2.5m\nTiled floor and backsplash, oak kitchen units, formica worktop\n\nUtility Room - 2.5m x 1.4m\nTiled floor, plumbed for washing machine\n\nBack Hallway - 2.5m x 1.0m\nTiled floor\n\nBathroom - 2.5m x 1.5m\nTiled floor, bath/shower, wc, whb\n\nBedroom One - 5.0m x 2.5m\nWooden floor, dual aspect, curtains\n\nBedroom Two - 5.0m x 2.8m\nConcrete floor, dual aspect, fireplace\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Two bedroom detached cottage </li><li>Set on a site of approximately 0.47 acres</li><li>Property requires modernisation and upgrades throughout</li><li>Potential for all available refurbishment grants</li><li>Convenient to Westport and Newport towns</li><li>Derelict stone outbuilding included</ul>"
